@startuml
title Back office — session bootstrap + shell (BoGuard)

actor Staff
participant "NGINX" as NGINX
participant "FE (Next.js BO)" as FE
participant "BE (Django/DRF)" as BE
database "DB (PostgreSQL)" as DB

' The BO is the (bo) route group of the single Next.js app (ADR 0005),
' served under one domain via NGINX (/ -> client, /bo -> back office).

== Log in (same SMS OTP flow as the client app) ==
Staff -> FE : open /bo, log in
note over FE, BE
  Identical request/verify/session flow as login-otp.puml
  (ADR 0002 & 0004) — staff and admin use POST /bo/v1/auth/otp/request
  + /bo/v1/auth/otp/verify. Only authorization differs downstream.
end note
BE --> FE : 200 + Set-Cookie: sessionid (HttpOnly)

== Guard the shell ==
Staff -> FE : load /bo
FE -> NGINX : GET /bo/v1/auth/me/ (Cookie: sessionid)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  users.views.CurrentUserView
  AuthN: SessionAuthentication; permission IsAuthenticated
end note
BE -> DB : SELECT user
BE --> FE : 200 (UserSerializer — includes role)
note right of FE
  BoGuard gates on role in {staff, admin}; a client is redirected out.
  FE guard is UX only — see note below.
end note

== Admin picks the active staff context ==
Staff -> FE : (admin) choose staff to manage
FE -> NGINX : GET /v1/staff/
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  users.views.StaffPublicListView (AllowAny)
  users.selectors.list_staff(bookable_only=True)
  Admin selects a staff_id used to scope BO calls
  (schedules, appointments, reports). Staff manage only themselves.
end note
BE -> DB : SELECT users_user (role=staff, is_active)
BE --> FE : 200 (StaffPublicSerializer[])
FE --> Staff : BO shell ready

note over Staff, DB
  Authorization is enforced SERVER-SIDE on every /bo/v1/ endpoint
  via IsStaffMember (role staff/admin — common/permissions.py).
  The FE BoGuard is convenience/UX only; it is never the access control.
end note
@enduml
